"Five makers checked independently on 2026-11-20 - Chord, T+A, Gustard, Topping and Denafrips - and all five say the same thing: USB and I2S carry the device's full capability, while the whole S/PDIF family (coaxial, optical, AES/EBU) stops at 24-bit/192 kHz and carries DSD only over DoP, to DSD64. The DoP figure is not an extra fact: 192 kHz divided by 16 IS DSD64, which is what the engine derives, so the makers and the arithmetic agree without consulting each other. The one exception found is Chord's BNC coaxial at 384 kHz. This regularity is RECORDED, not generalised: devices whose sheets were not found carry no input block rather than an assumed one, because a pattern across five devices is a good reason to go and look and a bad reason to stop looking."
